  <div class="meta"><time datetime="2026-09-24">Sep 24, 2026</time><span class="pages">82 pages</span><a class="badge fam" href="number-theory.html#f002" title="The full BSD formula from low Selmer corank">No. 002</a></div>
  <div class="abstract">We prove the Selmer converse in coranks zero and one for every elliptic curve over ℚ and every prime <i>p</i>: if the full <i>p</i>-power Selmer group has ℤ<sub><i>p</i></sub>-corank \(r\in\{0,1\}\), then the analytic and Mordell–Weil ranks both equal <i>r</i>, and the entire Tate–Shafarevich group is finite. As an application at the additive prime 3, we prove that for every prime \(\ell\equiv4,7,8\pmod9\), the cubic \(X^3+Y^3=\ell Z^3\) has analytic and Mordell–Weil rank one and finite Tate–Shafarevich group. In particular, every such <i>ℓ</i> is a sum of two rational cubes.</div>
