  <div class="abstract">We prove a uniform interior \(C^{1,\alpha_d}\) estimate for bounded infinity-harmonic functions in every dimension <i>d</i> ≥ 3. For some \(\alpha_d\in(0,1/3]\) depending only on the dimension, the gradient's supremum norm and <i>α</i><sub><i>d</i></sub>-Hölder seminorm on <i>B</i><sub>1/2</sub> are bounded by a dimension-dependent constant times the oscillation on <i>B</i><sub>1</sub>. The exponent is not explicit, and no endpoint or boundary regularity claim is made. In particular, infinity-harmonic functions are locally <i>C</i><sup>1</sup> on every open subset of ℝ<sup><i>d</i></sup>, for <i>d</i> ≥ 3.</div>
